Appendix A-യിലെ day axis-ിൽ നിന്ന് അഞ്ച് workCounts ഒരുമിച്ച് കണക്കാക്കുന്ന clean Stage 1 പരീക്ഷണം. input raw action day, target day. output ക്രമം action dayCount, target dayCount, chronological distance, connection, direction. direction mapping: target പഴയതെങ്കിൽ 1, same day 2, target മുന്നിലുള്ളത് 3.

Hamlet, raw action day സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Romeo, raw target day സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Macbeth, Foundation day സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Ophelia, action dayCount സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Othello, target dayCount സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Lady Macbeth, chronological distance സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Portia, connection സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Cordelia, direction സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Prospero, assignment, input, output, branching സഹായിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Miranda, Foundation constant നിർമ്മിക്കാൻ സഹായിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.

Act I: input-ും Foundation constant-ും.

Scene I: raw days വായിക്കുന്നു.
[Enter Prospero and Hamlet]
Prospero: Listen to your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Romeo]
Prospero: Listen to your heart.
[Exeunt]

Scene II: Foundation day -15055671 നിർമ്മിക്കുന്നു.
[Enter Macbeth and Miranda]
Miranda:
 You are a hero.
 You are as good as the sum of the product of yourself and the sum of a big big big hero and a big hero and the sum of a big big hero and a hero.
 You are as good as the product of yourself and the sum of a big big big hero and a big hero.
 You are as good as the sum of the product of yourself and the sum of a big big big hero and a big hero and the sum of a big big hero and a hero.
 You are as good as the sum of the product of yourself and the sum of a big big big hero and a big hero and the sum of a big big hero and a hero.
 You are as good as the sum of the product of yourself and the sum of a big big big hero and a big hero and the sum of a big big hero and a big hero.
 You are as good as the sum of the product of yourself and the sum of a big big big hero and a big hero and the sum of a big big hero and the sum of a big hero and a hero.
 You are as good as the sum of the product of yourself and the sum of a big big big hero and a big hero and a hero.
 You are as good as the difference between nothing and yourself.
Macbeth: You are as good as Miranda.
[Exeunt]

Act II: action dayCount.

Scene I: Foundation-നോട് action day താരതമ്യം ചെയ്യുന്നു.
[Enter Hamlet and Prospero]
Hamlet: Am I as good as Macbeth?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene II.
Hamlet: Am I better than Macbeth?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene III.
Prospero: Let us proceed to scene IV.

Scene II: Foundation dayCount = 1.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero: You are a hero. Let us proceed to act III.
[Exeunt]

Scene III: Foundation-ന് ശേഷം odd dayCount.
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of the product of the difference between Hamlet and Macbeth and a big hero and a hero. Let us proceed to act III.
[Exeunt]

Scene IV: Foundation-ന് മുമ്പ് even dayCount.
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero: You are as good as the product of the difference between Macbeth and Hamlet and a big hero.
[Exeunt]

Act III: target dayCount.

Scene I: Foundation-നോട് target day താരതമ്യം ചെയ്യുന്നു.
[Enter Romeo and Prospero]
Romeo: Am I as good as Macbeth?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene II.
Romeo: Am I better than Macbeth?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene III.
Prospero: Let us proceed to scene IV.

Scene II: Foundation target dayCount = 1.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Othello]
Prospero: You are a hero. Let us proceed to act IV.
[Exeunt]

Scene III: Foundation-ന് ശേഷം odd target dayCount.
[Enter Prospero and Othello]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of the product of the difference between Romeo and Macbeth and a big hero and a hero. Let us proceed to act IV.
[Exeunt]

Scene IV: Foundation-ന് മുമ്പ് even target dayCount.
[Enter Prospero and Othello]
Prospero: You are as good as the product of the difference between Macbeth and Romeo and a big hero.
[Exeunt]

Act IV: distance, connection, direction.

Scene I: chronological distance = absolute raw-day difference + 1.
[Enter Hamlet and Prospero]
Hamlet: Is Romeo better than Hamlet?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene II.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of the difference between Hamlet and Romeo and a hero. Let us proceed to scene III.
[Exeunt]

Scene II: target മുന്നിലുള്ളപ്പോൾ distance.
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of the difference between Romeo and Hamlet and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene III: connection = action + target dayCounts.
[Enter Prospero and Portia]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of Ophelia and Othello.
[Exeunt]

Scene IV: direction തിരഞ്ഞെടുക്കുന്നു.
[Enter Hamlet and Prospero]
Hamlet: Is Romeo worse than Hamlet?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene V.
Hamlet: Is Romeo as good as Hamlet?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene VI.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Cordelia]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of a big hero and a hero. Let us proceed to act V.
[Exeunt]

Scene V: target പഴയത്.
[Enter Prospero and Cordelia]
Prospero: You are a hero. Let us proceed to act V.
[Exeunt]

Scene VI: same day.
[Enter Prospero and Cordelia]
Prospero: You are a big hero.
[Exeunt]

